      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mounirlamouri/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "I'm not fully convinced. My rationale was to have the events firing and the promise resolving at the same place. Given that the promise resolving is [enqueued](https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-promise-resolve-functions) the position doesn't matter much.\n\nRegarding whether it would make sense to have \"if paused is false\" condition used to decide whether we reject the promises, what I wonder is whether this condition makes sense in the prose: it's obviously not implemented as is given that it's equivalent to simply setting the boolean. Also, we can't have a pending promise unless the `paused` attribute is false because calling `play()` will create a pending promise and state `paused` to false and calling `pause()` will reject the promise and set `paused` back to true.\n\nThis said, given that it has no concrete impact, I'm happy to apply the change if you feel strongly.\n",
