      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Well, OK, what I was going for was to put the rejection next to the reason for rejecting, which in my mind is the transition of paused from false to true, not really the emptied (or abort) event.\n\nSo, yeah, in order to not make it look like it's possible to have pending play promises if paused is true, I think moving it down into a branch would be nicer.\n\n(If the dedicated media source failure steps were made to also pause a similar setup there would be nice, but that's not for this PR.)\n",
